  "summary": "Independently checked all retained keys and alternatives against the cited local source passages, recalculated quantitative answers, compared with existing CVS stems, repaired distractors, synchronized linked QAs and exact locators, and validated the final question/catalog payload. Approval applies only to the five sealed files and these 59 original practice questions.",
  "checks": [
    "Guyton local extracted PDF pages were read for all retained physiology items; calculations were independently recomputed. In particular, PDF144 supports calibration, PDF151 lead axes/projection, PDF172 reentry, PDF227–229 afferent/resetting inference, PDF234 renal equilibrium, PDF258–261 return curves, PDF285 EF, PDF289 and175 S4/AF, PDF291–292 valves, and PDF299/302/304/305 shock mechanisms.",
    "Junqueira PDF286/printed275 was read for FDC retention, B-cell MHC-II processing and germinal-center variable-region changes. PDF297/300–302 (printed286/289–291) was read for splenic topology, central-arteriole eccentricity, afferent/efferent lymphatics and trabecular veins.",
    "Langman PDF232 text and PDF233 rendered image were inspected. The continuation establishes cisterna chyli dorsal to the retroperitoneal sac; the same rendered page establishes PROX1 specification, VEGFC–VEGFR3 sprouting, and the composite thoracic duct. No generated image or unverified OCR inference was used.",
    "Baseline stems compared: 88 physiology, 107 histology and 114 embryology. Neighboring prerequisite IDs in source-audit do not certify source support for all baseline questions. Two weak near-duplicate/elementary drafts were withdrawn.",
    "All 59 questions pass repository MCQ schema, contain four distinct options and individual option explanations including the keyed option. Every question belongs to exactly one objective; all concept/retrieval answers and source locators match the final MCQs. Concept groups contain 3–5 questions.",
    "The normalized CVS term2 catalog passes repository schema. CVS scope is book-extension (book-only evidence), not respiratory-only book-only schema vocabulary. All flat audit statuses conform to mapped/outside-scope/source-missing.",
    "Editorial challenge classification was recalibrated by required reasoning, not target counts: 30 challenge4 and29 core3. Reentry drug interaction, renal curve plus intake, paired hemorrhage/capacitance and septic resistance questions include explicit assumptions and independently checked arithmetic."
  ],
  "resolutionOfPriorFindings": [
